{number: 170}
{title: He Touched Me}
{key: Eb}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[Eb] Shackled by a heavy burden,
'Neath a [Bb7] load of guilt and [Eb] shame;
Then the hand of Jesus touched me,
And now I am no [Bb7] longer the [Eb] same.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
He [Bb7] touched me, O He [Eb] touched me,
And [F7] O the joy that floods my [Bb7] soul!
Something [Eb] happened, and now I [Ab] know,
He [Eb] touched me and [Bb7] made me [Eb] whole.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
Since I [Eb] met this blessed Savior,
Since He [Bb7] cleansed and made me [Eb] whole;
I will never cease to praise Him,
I'll shout it while e-[Bb7] ternity [Eb] rolls.
{end_of_verse}
